            <div xml:id="d478">

                <pb facs="0751" n="655" sameAs="frus:frus1931-41v01/pg655"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">793.94/15181: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Consul General at Shanghai</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Gauss</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                        State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Shanghai</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1939-07-08T16:00:00+08:00">July 8, 1939—4
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received July 8—8:45 a.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>576. Reference Department’s 186, July 7, 8 p.m., for Tokyo. I have taken action
                    as requested in last paragraph of this message. At the same time I have informed
                    Japanese Consul General that, according to information from the Commander of the
                    Yangtze Patrol, five bombs struck within two hundred yards of the U. S. S. <hi
                        rendition="#italic">Tutuila</hi> at Chungking during the recent air raids
                    there. Commander Yangtze Patrol has made representations to senior Japanese
                    naval officer here but I have deemed it appropriate to add this information in
                    my representations to the Japanese Consul General, and the Embassy at Tokyo may
                    wish to do likewise.</p>
                <p>Repeated to Tokyo, Chungking and Peiping.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Gauss</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
